                <pb facs="1537" n="1379" xml:id="pg1379"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Leishman to Consul-General
                    Bergholz</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Instructions allowing customs exemptions in favor of Beirut College mailed this
                    week to director in Beirut under No. 693. Am urging Porte for more general
                    orders in favor of all bona fide American institutions in Syria which are
                    entitled to exemption. Insist that director allow American institutions other
                    than college conditionally deposit custom duty, pending receipt of more general
                    orders which the Porte has promised to forward.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
